oss the data. As a result, this feature is unlikely to contribute to meaningful variation in the model and can be removed.\n```end\n\n```python\n# Explanation why the column `KURTOSIS_ABOUT_MAJOR_AXIS` is dropped\ndf.drop(columns=['KURTOSIS_ABOUT_MAJOR_AXIS'], inplace=True)\n# Reason: KURTOSIS_ABOUT_MAJOR_AXIS has a very narrow range [176, 204] and low variance (6.11), suggesting it doesn't add much distinguishing information for classification and is better excluded from the model.\n```end", "```python\n# 1. Log Transformation of Highly Skewed Features: \n# Apply logarithm transformation to highly skewed features such as SCALED_VARIANCE_ALONG_MINOR_AXIS, SCALED_RADIUS_OF_GYRATION, RADIUS_RATIO, and SCATTER_RATIO.\n# Usefulness: Log transformation can normalize highly skewed data and reduce the influence of large outliers while retaining a meaningful distinction between vehicle classes.\n\ndf['LOG_SCALED_VARIANCE_MINOR'] = np.log(df['SCALED_VARIANCE_ALONG_MINOR_AXIS'] + 1)\ndf['LOG_SCALED_RADIUS_OF_GYRATION'] = np.log(df['SCALED_RADIUS_OF_GYRATION'] + 1)\ndf['LOG_RADIUS_RATIO'] = np.log(df['RADIUS_RATIO'] + 1)\ndf['LOG_SCATTER_RATIO'] = np.log(df['SCATTER_RATIO'] + 1)\n```end\n\n```python\n# 2. Interaction Feature: Product of PR.AXIS_ASPECT_RATIO and MAX.LENGTH_ASPECT_RATIO\n# Create a new feature by multiplying PR.AXIS_ASPECT_RATIO and MAX.LENGTH_ASPECT_RATIO to model their combined effect on shape similarity.\n# Usefulness: Vehicles with different aspect ratios (e.g., VAN vs. SAAB) might have unique combinations of these ratios that are better captured by their product.\n\ndf['AXIS_PRODUCT'] = df['PR.AXIS_ASPECT_RATIO'] * df['MAX.LENGTH_ASPECT_RATIO']\n```end\n\n```python\n# 3. Normalize PR.AXIS_RECTANGULARITY and MAX.LENGTH_RECTANGULARITY via Z-score Normalization\n# Apply z-score normalization to PR.AXIS_RECTANGULARITY and MAX.LENGTH_RECTANGULARITY.\n# Usefulness: Both features relate to the rectangular dimensions of the silhouettes. Z-scoring these ensures unif